1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,200
 And what else do we have?

2
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:03,000
 We can also add up reference images.

3
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:06,280
 So what reference images are is basically images

4
00:00:06,280 --> 00:00:11,160
 that we can add in order to either include

5
00:00:11,160 --> 00:00:15,800
 in the generated result or inspire the bot.

6
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:18,840
 So for example, let's say that we want to create

7
00:00:18,840 --> 00:00:23,120
 an image, similar to another image that we already have,

8
00:00:23,120 --> 00:00:25,080
 or we've seen somewhere.

9
00:00:25,080 --> 00:00:28,200
 We can just add that image over here, upload it over here.

10
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:30,760
 And it will be used as a reference image.

11
00:00:30,760 --> 00:00:33,760
 Or for example, we want to add a certain logo

12
00:00:33,760 --> 00:00:37,600
 of our company in the generated image in a certain part, right?

13
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:40,040
 So we can use this reference image part

14
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:43,720
 in order to give the AI bot our photo.

15
00:00:43,720 --> 00:00:47,320
 And that photo will be used when it comes to generating

16
00:00:47,320 --> 00:00:49,440
 the end result that we want.

17
00:00:49,440 --> 00:00:51,400
 So this is also reference images.

18
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:53,200
 We can click on Upload Image.

19
00:00:53,200 --> 00:00:57,640
 And we can add our reference images over here, close this one.

